      },
      "message": "feat(cl,motion,post,app,ui): Probe operation - face, edge, corner and bore/boss centre finding\n\nA touch-probe tool kind (stylus ball + length, PRB-0400 in the starter\ncatalog) and a Probe operation seated at 13 to close the Drilling run\n(v50 -> v51 pin rung). Modes: face (+-X/+-Y/-Z), edge, outside corner\n(two touches), bore and boss centre (four touches). Each touch is a\nfast seek, a back-off and a slow measuring re-probe; the path opens with\na positioning rapid and the touches ride Toolpath::probes (cl::ProbeTouch),\nfiled in the path cache.\n\nThe post writes TOUCH / RETREAT / FOUND records: fanuc.cps voices them\nas G38.2 (NIST RS274NGC), an incremental G91 back-off, the deviation and\nits tolerance stop (#3000) and either G10 L2 Pn (set G54..G59) or a\n#3006 operator stop; a probe section starts no spindle or coolant. A\nscript without onProbeMove / onProbeRetreat / onProbeResult refuses the\nop by name. The stylus path is judged as protected moves against the\nmodel (a ball nearer than its radius anywhere is a Gouge, holding the\npost); probe ops remove no stock. Op page with an original icon.\n\nOwed: creating the op from a picked face/edge/vertex/cylinder (the\ncontact is typed today), the stylus shank in the protected-move law,\nprobing hooks for the other dialects.\n\nRefs #108\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
