      "message": "fix(post,app): Fanuc probing as G31 skip with macro B; Probe appends a stable kind id\n\nReview fixes on the #108 slice:\n\n- fanuc.cps writes the probing moves as the G31 skip function (Fanuc's\n  published operator documentation, custom macro B) instead of G38.2,\n  which a Fanuc control does not take. The skip position is read from\n  #5061-#5063; each skip block is followed by a no-contact check that\n  alarms (#3000=2), since G31 ends silently at its target when no signal\n  fires. The incremental back-off, tolerance stop and G10 L2 offset set\n  stay. Golden and test renamed (bore_centre_posts_g31_skips_on_the_generic_dialect).\n- Probe takes kind id 38 (appended) instead of seating at 13: stored\n  kind ids, digest tags and ribbon pins no longer move, the v51 format\n  rung and pin migration are dropped (files stay v50), and older\n  projects load with no op going Stale. The menu lists it in the\n  Drilling section by display order; the ribbon laws ask for table\n  order within a section instead of a contiguous run.\n\nFollow-ups filed: #171, #172, #173, #174.\n\nRefs #108\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
