        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-08T03:32:46Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(probe): program the stylus tip, not the ball centre\n\nThe probe path stated the ball centre while every other ball tool\nstates the tip, and a spindle probe's length register is gauged to the\nball's bottom. The default -Z face op therefore read every face r high\n(alarming on tolerance 0.5), and with a looser tolerance G10 L2 moved\nthe work zero r into the part - every following op cut r too deep.\n\nprobe_cycle still plans on the ball centre and now lays every move\npoint and probe target down at the tip (centre - r along +Z); the safe\nplane is a tip height. stylus_hits sweeps the ball about each point\nraised by r, so the judged geometry is unchanged. A -Z touch on a face\nat Z 20 now posts G31 Z15 (overtravel 5) and expects its trip at Z 20.\n\nPinned by probe_op::the_posted_g31_z_is_the_tip_at_the_expected_contact\n(face and bore-centre modes); the probe_bore_centre golden moves every\nZ 2 mm down except the safe plane. Decision in docs/decisions/108-probe.md.\n\nRefs #108\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
